  Disambiguation: this file's own `Principles:` section above
  (SeparationOfConcerns/SingleSourceOfTruth/ExplicitReference/Locality/
  NoDuplication/Traceability/HumanControl) is about how .sdd's own
  components relate to each other. It is unrelated to and unchanged by
  ./principles.sdd, which is about how real project code should be
  architected (domain boundaries, dependency direction, coupling). The
  near-identical naming (`Principles:` section here vs. `principles.sdd`
  file there) is coincidental, not a shared concept — do not merge them.

